cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "Concurrency-Safe Real-Time Course Registration: An Experimental Evaluation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chitakana
    given-names: Kishan Phani
date-released: 2026-10-29
license: MIT
keywords:
  - concurrency control
  - PostgreSQL
  - row-level locking
  - server-sent events
  - design of experiments
  - Go
  - React
abstract: >-
  A Go/PostgreSQL course-registration service with a live React dashboard over
  Server-Sent Events, evaluated in a randomised, repeated experiment (30 trials
  per cell). Row locking removed seat over-allocation (0/120 vs 120/120 trials)
  at a cost of 3-11 ms per request; SSE delivered changes in ~4 ms median versus
  161 ms and 1,626 ms for 500 ms and 2 s polling.
